{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_001_modular_monolith", "label": "ADR 001: Modular monolith with explicit ports", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/001-modular-monolith.md", "source_location": "1-45", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Historical entry points accumulated business rules and infrastructure concerns so a small feature required coordinated edits across unrelated files; a modular monolith with explicit ports keeps one deployable product while restoring dependency direction."}, {"id": "docs_adr_001_ports_and_adapters", "label": "Ports-and-adapters dependency direction (UI/IPC -> application -> domain <- infrastructure)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/001-modular-monolith.md", "source_location": "16-28", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Domain behavior must be reusable by desktop and mobile and native/cloud integrations must be replaceable in tests, so adapters implement core ports instead of the domain importing infrastructure."}, {"id": "docs_adr_001_vertical_slice_migration", "label": "Vertical-slice migration of existing code", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/001-modular-monolith.md", "source_location": "30-31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Moving files without first separating responsibilities is intentionally avoided, so each slice migrates behavior with temporary compatibility adapters rather than a risky bulk move."}, {"id": "docs_adr_001_window_api_contract", "label": "window.api as the single bridge contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/001-modular-monolith.md", "source_location": "28", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_001_modular_monolith", "target": "docs_adr_001_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "references", "confidence